\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {I clattered down the stairs, the smell of dried herbs and old wood getting stronger with every step. The shop was already alive\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 Lydia buried in her research notes at the back table, muttering to herself like the fate of the world depended on her handwriting, and Markus standing behind the counter looking like someone had just asked him to wrestle a bear.}
\par\plain {Markus was hard to miss. Big guy, broad shoulders, could probably lift a barrel of mandrake root without breaking a sweat. But shy as they came. We\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been friends back in our Liese Academy days, though \u8220\'93friends\u8221\'94 there mostly meant hiding from other students in the library and trading notes.}
\par\plain {I adjusted my satchel, tugged my newsboy cap into place, and leaned on the counter. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You sure you\u8217\'92ve got inventory and delivery today? That\u8217\'92s usually my circus.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Markus glanced up from the ledger, nervous smile on his face. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve already got inventory sorted. Delivery should be the same, right?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yeah, pretty much,\u8221\'94 I said, giving him a half-grin. \u8220\'93Just make sure to note things down properly. I\u8217\'92ll swing by the post office once I\u8217\'92m done with Torrie, yeah?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Okay,\u8221\'94 he said, nodding a little too earnestly. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll try my best.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I patted his arm\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 it was like patting a tree trunk. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re the man, Markus.\u8221\'94 I smiled, stepping back toward the door. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be back. Shouldn\u8217\'92t be that long.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain }